[COMMENTS]
STATION,Velocity area station in a flashy catchment. GENERAL: Velocity area station. STATION HYDROMETRY: The control is a compound weir of the Clyde River Purification Board design with two outer broad-crested sections straddling a rectangular flume style low flow channel. Archive notes describe the breakpoint of the low flow notch is at 0.36m and the structure drowns out at 1.5m. The weir suffered from erosion, and records describe the 1990 spates as being of particular affect. By 2023 the base of the low flow section was worn down to the concrete rebars, prompting some repair work between 19/07/2023 ad 24/10/2023. These repair works replaced the low flow channel and added a concrete layer (100mm) on top of the existing downstream aprons, increasing their height by 0.100m. The crest height of the two side sections weas unaltered during these works. The gauge zero was inadvertently changed after the installation of a new ramp gauge in 2002. The exact date and size of shift is pending further investigation of SEPA records but gauging deviations indicate it was lowered in the order of 0.060m and the corresponding rating start date suggests it happened on 11/09/2002. The ramp was replaced again in conjunction with weir repair works between July and October 2023, with no datum shift. Peak flow rating derived from current meter gaugings up to 1.830, with a measured flow of 50.6 cumecs. All flows are contained in the channel. FLOW RECORD: Some monthly naturalised flows available (1970-74). Full period of record peak flow data reviewed and released in August 2025 (WINFAP Files v14). FLOW REGIME: Flashy response. Minimal effluent returns affecting low flows.
CATCHMENT,Catchment topography is >1/3 lowland, <2/3 upland, draining the Campsie Fells. Carboniferous series (principally the Scottish Carboniferous L'st) dominate the bedrock - overlain by mixed superficial deposits. Sparsely populated. Landuse mainly rough pasture and improved pasture in lower parts; some forestry. No significant lochs or storages. No significant catchment changes known.
Qmed Suitability,Well gauged to QMED.
Pooling Suitability,A decent range of gaugings and flows contained in channel.
[END]
